    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2101.09448v1</id>
    <title>Classification by girth of three-dimensional algebraically defined monomial graphs over the real numbers</title>
    <updated>2021-01-23T07:43:28Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.09448v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2101.09448v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>For positive integers $s,t,u,v$, we define a bipartite graph $Γ_{\mathbb{R}}(X^s Y^t,X^u Y^v)$ where each partite set is a copy of $\mathbb{R}^3$, and a vertex $(a_1,a_2,a_3)$ in the first partite set is adjacent to a vertex $[x_1,x_2,x_3]$ in the second partite set if and only if
  \[
  a_2 + x_2 = a_1^s x_1^t
  \quad
  \text{and}
  \quad
  a_3+x_3=a_1^ux_1^v.
  \] In this paper, we classify all such graphs according to girth.</summary>
